<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net6.0;net7.0;net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>

		<!-- Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions 10.0.12 declares net6.0/net7.0
		     as "not tested" (both are EOL runtimes) but its assembly is netstandard2.0-compatible
		     and functions correctly there: verified via an actual runtime smoke test (DI container
		     built, AddAutoMapperLite resolved, a real Map<T> call executed and asserted) on net6.0,
		     not just assumed. Suppressed as a known-benign policy warning, not a real break. -->
		<SuppressTfmSupportBuildWarnings>true</SuppressTfmSupportBuildWarnings>

		<!-- NuGet Metadata -->
		<PackageId>AutoMapperLite</PackageId>
		<Version>4.4.1</Version>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>
			AutoMapperLite 4.4.1 — current official release; all prior versions are deprecated.

			• Fixed: a ForPath mapping targeting a leaf property that legitimately resolves to
			  null (e.g. an optional string) either lost that null to a freshly-constructed
			  instance, or — for a leaf type with no public parameterless constructor reachable
			  via reflection, most commonly string itself — threw InvalidOperationException
			  outright. The nested-path walk tried to descend one segment past the actual leaf;
			  only intermediate segments need that.
			• Added: same-name nested collection destination *properties* now also accept an
			  array (T[]) destination, matching the array support the top-level
			  Map&lt;TDestination&gt;(object) API already had since 4.4.0. Previously an
			  array-typed nested collection property was silently left unmapped even when a map
			  was registered for the item types; it is now populated the same way a List&lt;T&gt;-
			  or interface-typed nested collection property already was. Purely additive — no
			  existing mapping output changes, since this only fills in a property that was
			  previously always left at its default.
			• Documentation: corrected several stale claims left over from before the 4.4.0
			  mapping-engine redesign — destination construction is described as a compiled
			  constructor call (Expression.New) rather than Activator.CreateInstance in the
			  guide/FAQ, the home page's comparison FAQ answer no longer claims AutoMapperLite
			  trails AutoMapper on collections (it has beaten AutoMapper there since 4.4.0), and
			  SECURITY.md's supported-version table no longer references 4.2.x, a version that
			  was never published to NuGet (see CHANGELOG.md/CLAUDE.md for the verified publish
			  history), and the performance page no longer overstates Activator.CreateInstance's
			  elimination (it still backs the interpreted ForPath walk and the untyped
			  collection-dispatch fallback, just not the compiled per-property path). No
			  code-behavior changes from the documentation fixes.
			• No public API breaking changes since 4.0.2.

			Previous (4.4.0): mapping engine and performance redesign — each source/destination
			type pair now compiles into a cached delegate via System.Linq.Expressions on first
			use instead of being interpreted through reflection; added
			IMapper.Map&lt;TSource,TDestination&gt;(TSource) and broader collection-destination
			support (T[], IList&lt;T&gt;, ICollection&lt;T&gt;, IReadOnlyList&lt;T&gt;,
			IReadOnlyCollection&lt;T&gt;, IEnumerable&lt;T&gt;); fixed a collection-loop
			interface-dispatch cost, flipping AutoMapperLite from trailing AutoMapper on
			collection mapping to beating it at every size from 1,000 items upward. See
			docs/performance.html and docs/changelog.html for full measured results and history.
		</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<Authors>Atik Hassan</Authors>
		<Company>AutoMapperLite</Company>
		<Description>AutoMapperLite is a lightweight object-to-object mapper for .NET — a small, dependency-minimal alternative to AutoMapper for mapping DTOs and entities. Each source/destination type pair is compiled into a cached delegate via System.Linq.Expressions on first use, rather than interpreted via reflection on every call. Targets net6.0 through net10.0. Features fluent CreateMap/ForMember/ForPath profiles for custom and nested member mapping, mapping to List&lt;T&gt;, arrays, and common collection interfaces (IList&lt;T&gt;, ICollection&lt;T&gt;, IReadOnlyList&lt;T&gt;, IEnumerable&lt;T&gt;), thread-safe configuration, and singleton-friendly dependency injection via AddAutoMapperLite. Built for projects that want a simple, dependency-minimal mapper without a large footprint; see the published benchmarks for exactly how it compares to AutoMapper and Mapster. Official site: https://automapperlite.atkhssn.info</Description>
		<PackageTags>mapper;object mapper;object mapping;dto mapper;dto mapping;entity mapping;automapper alternative;mapster alternative;dotnet mapper;csharp mapper;lightweight mapper;compiled mapping</PackageTags>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://automapperlite.atkhssn.info</PackageProjectUrl>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/atkhssn/AutoMapperLite</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<Copyright>© 2025-2026 Atik Hassan</Copyright>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<!-- Files to include in NuGet -->
		<None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
		<None Include="LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
		<None Include="icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="10.0.12" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="AutoMapperLite.Tests" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<Compile Remove="AutoMapperLite.Tests/**" />
		<Compile Remove="AutoMapperLite.Benchmarks/**" />
		<EmbeddedResource Remove="AutoMapperLite.Tests/**" />
		<EmbeddedResource Remove="AutoMapperLite.Benchmarks/**" />
		<None Remove="AutoMapperLite.Tests/**" />
		<None Remove="AutoMapperLite.Benchmarks/**" />
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>